@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT domain
IMPORT `g7-administrative-courts`

-- g7-tests-administrative-courts.l4: tests of section 62 (the Administrative Courts Law) and its meeting with section 56.
--
-- Written by ENCODER G7.  Expected values come from the SOURCE, decided before any run:
--   s.62  adds this Law to item 21 of the First Schedule to the Administrative Courts Law.  So the Law is listed; a
--         decision is one that can be taken to an Administrative Court only if it was made under the Law AND that
--         statute (out of scope, an input) gives the court jurisdiction.
--   s.56(a)  a final decision of the Commissioner under Chapter 6 can be appealed to the Magistrates' Court.
--   T39   a final decision of the Commissioner under Chapter 6 is within both: the Law does not say which governs.
--         Read additively, both courts are open; read with section 56 as the only route, only the Magistrates' Court.

§ `Tests of section 62`

§§ `The listing and the decision that can be taken to an Administrative Court`

#ASSERT `the Law is listed in item 21 of the First Schedule to the Administrative Courts Law, as section 62 adds it`

-- Made under the Law and the Administrative Courts Law gives jurisdiction: yes.
#ASSERT `s 62 — the decision can be taken to an Administrative Court` TRUE TRUE
-- Made under the Law but that statute gives no jurisdiction (the input says so): no.
#ASSERT NOT `s 62 — the decision can be taken to an Administrative Court` TRUE FALSE
-- Not made under the Law: the listing does not reach it, whatever that statute says.
#ASSERT NOT `s 62 — the decision can be taken to an Administrative Court` FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 62 — the decision can be taken to an Administrative Court` FALSE FALSE

§§ `Fora, reading section 62 as additional to section 56`

-- A final decision of the Commissioner under Chapter 6 that an Administrative Court can also hear: both fora.
#ASSERT `the fora for review of a decision, reading section 62 as additional to section 56` TRUE TRUE EQUALS LIST `the Magistrates' Court, on appeal under section 56`, `an Administrative Court, under the Administrative Courts Law as section 62 amends it`
-- A final decision of the Commissioner that no Administrative Court can hear: the Magistrates' Court only.
#ASSERT `the fora for review of a decision, reading section 62 as additional to section 56` TRUE FALSE EQUALS LIST `the Magistrates' Court, on appeal under section 56`
-- Any other decision under the Law that an Administrative Court can hear: that court only.
#ASSERT `the fora for review of a decision, reading section 62 as additional to section 56` FALSE TRUE EQUALS LIST `an Administrative Court, under the Administrative Courts Law as section 62 amends it`
-- A decision no forum is given for.
#ASSERT null (`the fora for review of a decision, reading section 62 as additional to section 56` FALSE FALSE)

§§ `Fora, reading section 56 as the only route for a final decision of the Commissioner`

-- The discriminating case: the Commissioner's final decision that an Administrative Court could also hear.
-- Only the Magistrates' Court is open on this reading; both are open on the other.
#ASSERT `the fora for review of a decision, reading section 56 as the only route for a final decision of the Commissioner` TRUE TRUE EQUALS LIST `the Magistrates' Court, on appeal under section 56`
#ASSERT `the fora for review of a decision, reading section 56 as the only route for a final decision of the Commissioner` TRUE FALSE EQUALS LIST `the Magistrates' Court, on appeal under section 56`
-- Where the decision is not the Commissioner's, the two readings agree.
#ASSERT `the fora for review of a decision, reading section 56 as the only route for a final decision of the Commissioner` FALSE TRUE EQUALS LIST `an Administrative Court, under the Administrative Courts Law as section 62 amends it`
#ASSERT null (`the fora for review of a decision, reading section 56 as the only route for a final decision of the Commissioner` FALSE FALSE)
